# Top-level .gitignore for the modules tree.
#
# Patterns are scoped to standard kbuild build outputs that get
# generated when `mka kernel` builds an external module via
# `make M=<this-dir>`. None of these belong in the source tree;
# all are regenerable from the .c/.h sources and the kernel.
#
# Confirmed against `git ls-files` at landing time: 0 currently-
# tracked files match these patterns.

# Compiled object files
*.o
*.o.d

# Per-module artifacts produced by modpost
*.ko
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.mod.o

# Kbuild metadata files
Module.symvers
modules.order

# Hidden command files kbuild writes alongside outputs
# (e.g. `.foo.o.cmd`, `.bar.ko.cmd`, `.modules.order.cmd`)
.*.cmd

# Don't ignore non-build dotfiles — only kbuild's `.<basename>.cmd`
# pattern. `.gitignore`, `.gitattributes`, etc. stay tracked because
# their basename doesn't match `*.cmd`.
